WEBVTT

00:02.669 --> 00:04.045
How about we divide and conquer?

00:04.129 --> 00:05.714
SAKAMOTO 15M, SHIN 10M, LU 5M
TOTAL: 30M

00:06.673 --> 00:08.925
Gambling is just luck, after all, right?

00:09.009 --> 00:12.512
No, there's gotta be a catch.
Wutang is the consigliere of the Lu clan.

00:12.595 --> 00:14.055
He's the brains of the group.

00:14.139 --> 00:18.351
I doubt he'd suggest this
if it were a simple game of luck.

00:18.435 --> 00:19.269
Indeed.

00:20.770 --> 00:23.398
Gambling may seem like games of chance,

00:23.481 --> 00:26.735
but in fact, they are games of calculation
based on shrewd psychological warfare.

00:27.652 --> 00:28.486
All in.

00:30.113 --> 00:32.240
Unlike hit men like you,

00:32.323 --> 00:35.869
we don't have the luxury
of leaving things to chance.

00:35.952 --> 00:37.787
Life in the mafia isn't that easy.

00:39.330 --> 00:41.791
The same guy took it all again!

00:41.875 --> 00:44.169
His personality is as bad as his hairdo.

00:45.253 --> 00:48.548
I shouldn't have agreed to this
in the heat of the moment!

00:48.631 --> 00:50.133
It's the same with hit men.

00:50.967 --> 00:54.387
The ones who let fate take its course
die first.

00:56.681 --> 00:59.184
Show me what you idiots can come up with.

01:00.351 --> 01:02.604
<i>I will get my lady back.</i>

01:02.687 --> 01:05.023
<i>I'll bet everything on it.</i>

01:06.858 --> 01:08.902
WIN MORE THAN WUTANG AT THE CASINO!

02:40.910 --> 02:42.954
I still don't know the rules, though.

02:43.037 --> 02:44.372
CASINO BATTLE

02:44.455 --> 02:46.624
Well, no use worrying now.

02:46.708 --> 02:50.128
<i>I'll just give it a try</i>
<i>and figure things out as I play.</i>

02:50.211 --> 02:51.045
Have a seat.

02:53.298 --> 02:56.259
<i>Never seen this kid before.</i>
<i>Must be a newbie.</i>

02:57.343 --> 02:58.678
<i>He's like a sitting duck.</i>

02:58.761 --> 03:01.723
<i>He looks like a guy you'd see</i>
<i>working at a run-down mom-and-pop shop.</i>

03:01.806 --> 03:03.892
<i>I'll squeeze him for all he's worth.</i>

03:03.975 --> 03:06.311
<i>I can hear you, assholes.</i>

03:06.853 --> 03:07.729
Let's begin.

03:11.190 --> 03:13.568
<i>I guess I look at the cards now?</i>

03:15.820 --> 03:16.821
Call.

03:16.905 --> 03:18.323
Raise, two million.

03:18.865 --> 03:20.283
I'll raise to four.

03:20.867 --> 03:22.911
<i>What does any of that mean?</i>

03:23.995 --> 03:25.455
There you are, Shin!

03:25.538 --> 03:27.749
Did you learn the rules?

03:28.249 --> 03:31.669
You have "uh-oh" written on your face!
Why didn't you learn the rules?!

03:31.753 --> 03:33.421
Shut up!

03:33.504 --> 03:36.466
I can't look anything up
'cause they took our smartphones.

03:36.549 --> 03:38.301
Don't embarrass me like this!

03:38.384 --> 03:41.679
We'd have a better chance if I play, then.
Give me the cards!

03:43.264 --> 03:45.308
<i>-So he is an amateur.</i>
-Let go.

03:45.391 --> 03:46.726
Stop it!

03:49.938 --> 03:50.772
Come on, hurry!

03:50.855 --> 03:53.566
<i>This kid got an ace and a king?</i>

03:53.650 --> 03:56.236
<i>No way, he could get a straight!</i>

03:56.319 --> 03:59.781
<i>Don't worry.</i>
<i>We can just bluff and he'll back out.</i>

04:00.365 --> 04:04.327
Sorry, kiddo, you're not gonna beat me
with cards like that.

04:04.410 --> 04:06.871
Though we won't stop you
if you want to call.

04:08.456 --> 04:10.083
Your bluff won't work on me.

04:11.459 --> 04:12.627
All in.

04:17.465 --> 04:18.549
SHIN +12M
TOTAL: 22M

04:18.633 --> 04:21.261
Hey dealer, how about
you deal the next hand face-up?

04:21.344 --> 04:23.763
That might save us some time.

04:23.846 --> 04:26.015
<i>How the hell did he do that?</i>

04:27.684 --> 04:29.435
Split.

04:29.519 --> 04:31.229
I'll go for another corner bet.

04:32.730 --> 04:34.065
<i>Looks like fatty's joining.</i>

04:35.400 --> 04:39.153
<i>All in on red? What's this fatty's deal?</i>

04:39.237 --> 04:41.072
<i>Maybe I'll keep one, just in case.</i>

04:42.323 --> 04:46.536
<i>So this is the fatty</i>
<i>Mr. Wutang was talking about.</i>

04:46.619 --> 04:47.996
<i>Tough luck.</i>

04:48.079 --> 04:52.125
<i>We have an electromagnet</i>
<i>that lets me control where the ball lands.</i>

04:52.208 --> 04:54.460
-Where will it land?
-Gimme one more!

04:58.881 --> 05:00.800
<i>And it's over.</i>

05:10.143 --> 05:12.353
<i>How in the world?</i>

05:13.521 --> 05:15.606
The fatty's got some guts!

05:15.690 --> 05:17.358
<i>Just meticulous control.</i>

05:17.442 --> 05:19.402
SAKAMOTO TOTAL: 29M

05:22.655 --> 05:25.658
Mr. Wutang, they're winning
hand over fist.

05:26.159 --> 05:27.577
Perhaps they're cheating.

05:28.161 --> 05:29.412
Do not intervene.

05:29.495 --> 05:31.664
I expected some degree of foul play.

05:31.748 --> 05:32.874
But…

05:32.957 --> 05:36.294
<i>Plus one, zero,</i>
<i>plus one, plus one, plus one.</i>

05:36.377 --> 05:39.422
<i>Minus one, zero,</i>
<i>minus one, plus one, plus one.</i>

05:39.505 --> 05:41.174
<i>Making the total plus four.</i>

05:41.257 --> 05:42.633
What would you like to do?

05:43.134 --> 05:43.968
Hit me.

05:48.765 --> 05:50.308
Blackjack!

05:50.391 --> 05:52.310
That guy with the braid is on a roll!

05:53.352 --> 05:56.481
<i>There it is. Mr. Wutang's</i>
<i>signature play style, counting.</i>

05:56.564 --> 06:00.735
<i>When he plays blackjack,</i>
<i>he memorizes the cards that have appeared</i>

06:00.818 --> 06:03.613
<i>to estimate the chances</i>
<i>of the next card being a ten.</i>

06:03.696 --> 06:04.989
<i>What a high-level skill.</i>

06:05.782 --> 06:09.035
<i>I will win. No matter what I have to do.</i>

06:09.911 --> 06:13.247
<i>You think you're better than us</i>
<i>just because you're smart?</i>

06:13.748 --> 06:17.460
All that matters in the mafia
is how strong you are!

06:17.543 --> 06:21.297
We don't need a wimp like you
in the Lu clan!

06:23.257 --> 06:25.218
Shit, it's Mr. Lu's daughter!

06:25.301 --> 06:26.552
Ow! Let's go.

06:28.012 --> 06:29.055
Are you okay?

06:29.847 --> 06:32.266
LU SHAOTANG
CLAN LEADER'S DAUGHTER, 8 YEARS OLD

06:32.350 --> 06:35.269
LU WUTANG
MAFIA APPRENTICE, 11 YEARS OLD

06:36.813 --> 06:37.772
Oh!

06:37.855 --> 06:40.525
So you're one of my relatives?

06:40.608 --> 06:43.277
There are so many of us in the Lu clan,
I never knew.

06:43.361 --> 06:46.447
Why were you letting them beat you up?

06:48.574 --> 06:50.785
Fighting back isn't the only way to fight.

06:50.868 --> 06:55.915
In that scenario, allowing them to win
and getting them in trouble later

06:55.998 --> 06:59.168
would damage them more in the end
than if I fought back.

07:00.795 --> 07:02.463
<i>What a weak excuse.</i>

07:03.506 --> 07:04.966
Hmm. You must be…

07:05.925 --> 07:07.468
really smart!

07:09.470 --> 07:14.350
Daddy told me
that everyone has at least one weapon.

07:14.434 --> 07:18.521
But that doesn't have to be the same thing
as other people.

07:19.647 --> 07:22.358
Your weapon must be your brain, Wutang.

07:23.609 --> 07:26.028
<i>For the first time in my life,</i>
<i>I felt accepted.</i>

07:27.947 --> 07:29.866
<i>I realized that I could be myself.</i>

07:29.949 --> 07:34.787
<i>I vowed to climb to the top my way</i>
<i>and stand beside her someday.</i>

07:36.497 --> 07:40.793
<i>Eventually, I came to be called</i>
<i>the brain of the organization.</i>

07:42.044 --> 07:44.547
<i>My gratitude to the clan is immeasurable.</i>

07:45.089 --> 07:49.302
<i>I'll eliminate anyone who gets in the way</i>
<i>of my lady's peaceful life.</i>

07:51.137 --> 07:54.599
I'll go first. 87,630 chips.

07:54.682 --> 07:56.184
WUTANG CHIP TOTAL: 87,630

07:56.267 --> 07:57.643
Damn, we're tied.

07:57.727 --> 07:58.895
SAKAMOTO'S CHIP TOTAL: 87,630

07:58.978 --> 08:00.688
Thank god we didn't lose.

08:01.856 --> 08:04.775
You did pretty good for imbeciles.

08:04.859 --> 08:06.235
Can we leave now?

08:06.319 --> 08:08.905
Hold up. We don't have a winner yet.

08:09.614 --> 08:12.825
Mr. Wutang, why not just shoot them?

08:12.909 --> 08:15.161
That won't be necessary. Back off.

08:15.244 --> 08:16.454
But sir--

08:16.537 --> 08:19.665
Did you not hear me? I said, back off.

08:22.543 --> 08:24.545
You'll play a game of poker with me.

08:24.629 --> 08:27.215
Poker? I don't know the rules.

08:27.298 --> 08:29.842
I didn't really get it, either.

08:31.302 --> 08:35.056
Then what game do you idiots know?

08:35.640 --> 08:37.642
Oh! I know a good one.

08:39.810 --> 08:43.397
It wouldn't be fair to play three to one,
so I'm adding two men to my team.

08:43.481 --> 08:45.358
The rules are simple.

08:45.441 --> 08:48.694
The team with the person
who has the joker at the end loses.

08:48.778 --> 08:50.446
Basically, Old Maid. Right?

08:50.530 --> 08:53.449
Now we're talking!
These simple games are the best.

08:53.533 --> 08:55.451
It's so exciting.

08:55.535 --> 08:57.537
I used to play this with my girls.

08:58.120 --> 09:00.206
<i>Do they have no sense of suspense?</i>

09:00.289 --> 09:01.832
<i>Idiot.</i>

09:01.916 --> 09:05.586
<i>This will be an easy win</i>
<i>for a mind-reader like me.</i>

09:06.254 --> 09:08.714
<i>This is my chance to impress Mr. Sakamoto!</i>

09:08.798 --> 09:10.508
Let's begin.

09:11.050 --> 09:14.428
<i>Let's see, who has the joker?</i>

09:14.512 --> 09:16.889
<i>Which one of you is the most nervous…</i>

09:20.560 --> 09:22.853
<i>Seriously, Lu?!</i>

09:33.114 --> 09:34.657
<i>It's all over her face too.</i>

09:35.908 --> 09:38.744
You have always been so honest, my lady.

09:39.704 --> 09:42.039
However, I will not go easy on you.

09:50.172 --> 09:51.215
This one.

09:52.925 --> 09:57.346
I have purged the joker from your hands!
You're safe now, my lady.

09:58.014 --> 09:59.932
<i>That's not how you play this game!</i>

10:00.808 --> 10:03.269
Now it's your turn. Take a card.

10:04.103 --> 10:06.105
Hmm, which one should I take?

10:06.188 --> 10:08.899
<i>Psych! I'll know which one to take</i>
<i>once I read his--</i>

10:08.983 --> 10:11.360
You can read minds, right?

10:12.361 --> 10:15.156
The human mind
has three types of consciousness.

10:15.239 --> 10:18.326
Verbalized consciousness,
the preconscious,

10:18.409 --> 10:22.121
and the subconscious,
like habits or reflexes.

10:23.039 --> 10:25.750
I wonder, how far can you read?

10:27.835 --> 10:32.757
Pick a card.
If my intuition is right, you'll lose.

10:32.840 --> 10:34.425
<i>What's he talking about?</i>

10:34.508 --> 10:37.428
<i>He's just messing with me.</i>
<i>I'm sure it's a bluff.</i>

10:42.600 --> 10:46.896
<i>Shin tried to read</i>
<i>everything in Wutang's mind.</i>

10:47.772 --> 10:48.939
<i>However,</i>

10:49.940 --> 10:54.278
<i>that was a dangerous act, like looking</i>
<i>at the sun through a magnifying glass.</i>

10:55.237 --> 10:59.617
<i>The excessive amount of information</i>
<i>caused Shin's brain to overheat.</i>

11:03.704 --> 11:06.707
Just as I thought.
You read the verbalized mind, don't you?

11:06.791 --> 11:08.209
Shin!

11:08.292 --> 11:10.127
SHIN - OUT OF THE GAME

11:11.629 --> 11:14.048
<i>What are we gonna do without Shin?</i>

11:20.096 --> 11:21.889
Hey, hurry up, fatty.

11:22.515 --> 11:23.849
<i>Hurry?</i>

11:23.933 --> 11:24.892
C'mon,

11:25.851 --> 11:29.230
keep it moving, would you?

11:29.772 --> 11:32.775
<i>Did he just take a card and then swap it?</i>

11:33.275 --> 11:34.110
Wait a second.

11:35.027 --> 11:36.862
What did you just do?

11:37.655 --> 11:40.825
If there's any sign of cheating again,
you're out of the game.

11:51.335 --> 11:54.338
Face your doom, hit man.

11:59.885 --> 12:03.180
Your poker face is impressive
but not enough to fool me.

12:03.264 --> 12:06.475
Your eyes glanced toward this card,
ever so slightly.

12:06.559 --> 12:10.855
We humans have a tendency
to look at the thing we're trying to hide.

12:11.439 --> 12:12.481
Take a card, then.

12:13.774 --> 12:16.110
It's game over.

12:23.909 --> 12:25.327
My god!

12:25.911 --> 12:29.081
His grip strength is insane!

12:29.165 --> 12:32.501
Sorry about that.
I was holding on too tight.

12:36.464 --> 12:38.424
Damn, you switched cards.

12:38.507 --> 12:40.676
I believe it's my turn.

12:43.888 --> 12:46.640
Hey, what do you think you're--

12:48.100 --> 12:49.310
What is this?

12:49.393 --> 12:51.395
We came all the way to Japan

12:51.479 --> 12:54.190
just for you and your stupid game.

12:54.273 --> 12:55.983
We can't take it anymore!

12:56.066 --> 12:57.902
We're the mafia.

12:57.985 --> 12:59.945
If we want something, we take it.

13:00.029 --> 13:02.573
The way you do things is so dorky!

13:02.656 --> 13:05.326
Yeah, he's right! You nerd!

13:05.951 --> 13:06.827
What's going on?

13:07.411 --> 13:10.039
Oh my god, they totally hate him.

13:11.749 --> 13:15.002
<i>It's just like when I was young.</i>

13:16.420 --> 13:18.214
<i>Everything I've done…</i>

13:19.507 --> 13:20.674
<i>It was all worthless.</i>

13:23.219 --> 13:24.553
Mutiny?

13:25.262 --> 13:28.057
What a boring death for a mafia member.

13:28.724 --> 13:29.725
<i>I guess this is it.</i>

13:32.102 --> 13:34.396
You're giving up rather easily.

13:35.397 --> 13:39.318
Don't you want to impress your crush?

13:43.656 --> 13:45.741
<i>You must be really smart!</i>

13:46.283 --> 13:49.078
<i>Your weapon must be your brain, Wutang.</i>

13:50.538 --> 13:54.875
<i>That's it! I will win, my way.</i>

13:56.669 --> 13:59.088
Stop meddling, Taro Sakamoto.

13:59.672 --> 14:03.300
Their arms were supposed to blow up
when they fired those guns.

14:04.176 --> 14:08.597
Did you think that I, of all people,
wouldn't notice an uprising?

14:09.431 --> 14:12.851
I rigged your guns to explode when fired.

14:14.186 --> 14:17.356
I'm counting on you, Taro Sakamoto.

14:55.185 --> 14:58.647
Morons. Bluffing is gambling 101.

14:59.231 --> 15:00.649
<i>He was lying?</i>

15:01.317 --> 15:02.151
Sakamoto,

15:02.776 --> 15:04.612
you've won this fight.

15:05.487 --> 15:07.740
I've put my lady in harm's way.

15:08.574 --> 15:10.326
I don't deserve to protect her.

15:11.327 --> 15:12.411
So…

15:12.494 --> 15:15.080
I don't know what you deserve,

15:15.831 --> 15:19.293
but I do know what it's like
to want to protect those dear to you.

15:22.671 --> 15:23.505
Of course.

15:24.381 --> 15:26.258
SAKAMOTO'S

15:26.342 --> 15:28.844
So, Sakamoto, as promised,

15:28.928 --> 15:32.306
I'll give you information
on the person who put the bounty on you.

15:32.389 --> 15:33.515
THE IKORAI TIMES

15:33.599 --> 15:35.559
Are you even listening?

15:35.643 --> 15:37.519
Yeah, sure we are.

15:37.603 --> 15:40.314
Could you do something
while you talk, Wutang?

15:40.397 --> 15:43.943
We have a lot of work to catch up on
because of you.

15:44.026 --> 15:47.154
You look pretty good in that apron.

15:48.489 --> 15:52.409
I can't believe you're making me,
a mafia consigliere, work for you.

15:52.493 --> 15:54.995
I will be invoicing you for every hour.

15:55.579 --> 15:56.413
Anyway…

15:57.164 --> 15:58.332
Sakamoto,

15:58.415 --> 16:01.001
have you heard of a person called Slur?

16:04.004 --> 16:05.547
<i>The hit man killer?</i>

16:06.131 --> 16:08.300
So you have heard of them.

16:08.384 --> 16:11.428
Young man, could you ring these up for me?

16:12.179 --> 16:15.391
That's who put the bounty on your head.

16:15.933 --> 16:17.434
-But we already…
-Need a bag?

16:17.518 --> 16:19.478
-…had a hunch it was Slur.
-No thanks.

16:19.561 --> 16:21.814
Do you know Slur's name?
Or where they are?

16:22.398 --> 16:28.362
Unfortunately, no one has any information
to identify the person known as "Slur."

16:28.946 --> 16:31.073
You have got to be kidding me.

16:31.156 --> 16:33.409
What did we even fight for?

16:34.034 --> 16:35.035
A complete waste.

16:35.119 --> 16:37.538
I'm not finished yet!

16:38.330 --> 16:42.042
There are a lot of mysteries,
but I do have a few trails leading to him.

16:43.419 --> 16:44.503
What do you mean?

16:45.337 --> 16:50.551
A few days ago, a prison located
in Southeast Asia reported some murders.

16:51.927 --> 16:54.847
<i>Four inmates on death row</i>
<i>for first-degree murder were killed.</i>

16:55.431 --> 16:57.683
<i>The faces were burned off of the bodies,</i>

16:57.766 --> 17:00.436
<i>and an "X" was painted in blood</i>
<i>on the wall.</i>

17:00.519 --> 17:03.480
Does that mean Slur killed those inmates?

17:03.564 --> 17:05.441
But for what reason?

17:06.025 --> 17:10.446
An associate of mine who makes a living
buying and selling dead bodies told me

17:10.529 --> 17:14.450
that a few peculiar corpses
have been found in Japan recently.

17:15.701 --> 17:17.953
<i>One body was riddled with holes,</i>

17:18.620 --> 17:20.748
<i>one had all of its flesh scraped off,</i>

17:21.373 --> 17:23.333
<i>one was dismembered into pieces,</i>

17:24.209 --> 17:27.254
<i>and one was compressed into a small ball.</i>

17:28.589 --> 17:31.258
So? What do those bodies
have to do with this?

17:31.884 --> 17:36.263
These methods resemble those of the four
inmates who were supposedly killed.

17:37.806 --> 17:42.519
It's likely that the inmates on death row
escaped prison after faking their deaths

17:42.603 --> 17:44.605
<i>and are now hiding in Japan.</i>

17:45.314 --> 17:47.149
Whoa, look at those guys.

17:47.232 --> 17:49.068
That guy's huge! Is he a foreigner?

17:49.151 --> 17:51.361
Maybe he's an athlete. Or a pro fighter?

17:55.491 --> 17:57.576
What are they gawking at?

17:57.659 --> 17:59.495
It's like they're asking to be killed.

17:59.578 --> 18:00.996
DUMP - 180 VICTIMS

18:01.080 --> 18:03.707
MAN VOL. 2
ATONO MATSURI

18:03.791 --> 18:06.960
Japanese manga are hilarious.

18:07.044 --> 18:08.462
SAW - 64 VICTIMS

18:09.046 --> 18:11.340
Huh? There are pickles in my burger.

18:11.423 --> 18:13.050
But I asked for no pickles.

18:13.133 --> 18:15.844
I shouldn't have come to Japan.

18:15.928 --> 18:17.346
I want to die.

18:17.888 --> 18:19.306
APART - 206 VICTIMS

18:21.517 --> 18:24.019
Japanese burgers are tiny.

18:28.690 --> 18:30.109
MINIMALIST - 370 VICTIMS

18:31.443 --> 18:34.738
What are they gonna have us do anyway?

18:34.822 --> 18:39.076
C'mon, just chill out and wait.
Maybe you should read some manga.

18:40.077 --> 18:42.496
What are you doing over there?

18:42.579 --> 18:46.333
I made sure to tell them "no pickles."

18:46.416 --> 18:48.085
But there were pickles in it.

18:48.168 --> 18:50.045
So how am I supposed to believe

18:50.129 --> 18:52.965
there isn't anything else in here?

18:53.048 --> 18:55.592
God, what a whiny little brat.

19:05.185 --> 19:07.479
It's all the same if you just squash it.

19:08.272 --> 19:10.315
That was my Big Whack…

19:11.400 --> 19:12.734
I want to die.

19:12.818 --> 19:15.487
Sorry to keep you waiting.

19:15.571 --> 19:19.241
Are you the weirdo who let us escape?

19:19.908 --> 19:23.537
Thank you so much for coming all the way.

19:23.620 --> 19:25.455
Let's get right to business.

19:25.539 --> 19:26.373
NAGUMO
SAKAMOTO

19:26.456 --> 19:30.669
I'd like for you
to kill the people on this list.

19:31.712 --> 19:32.880
Who are they?

19:32.963 --> 19:38.760
They are detrimental to our organization.

19:39.428 --> 19:41.054
I couldn't care less.

19:41.138 --> 19:43.557
If I get to do what I want,
that's good enough.

19:44.516 --> 19:46.727
They all look so strong.

19:47.227 --> 19:50.522
This is it, this is how I'll die.
They'll tear me apart.

19:50.606 --> 19:53.400
Bleh. They're not even cute.

19:54.610 --> 19:57.404
I'd heard the Japanese are serious people,

19:57.487 --> 19:59.531
but I guess you do joke around sometimes.

20:00.115 --> 20:03.785
You can't expect me to believe
that this fatty is a problem for you.

20:04.828 --> 20:09.875
Not a single person on that list
should be underestimated.

20:10.417 --> 20:12.419
It could cost you your lives.

20:14.296 --> 20:17.966
You seriously think that,
if we're not careful,

20:18.717 --> 20:21.762
we could lose to this fatty and his posse?

20:29.102 --> 20:31.688
One month will be enough to kill them all.

20:38.904 --> 20:41.573
In a month, you bring us your next list.

20:44.910 --> 20:47.788
Or else we go on a killing spree in Japan.

20:53.418 --> 20:58.257
<i>They do not kill to make a living,</i>
<i>but rather, they live to kill.</i>

20:59.091 --> 21:01.843
<i>Unadulterated, pure evil.</i>

21:01.927 --> 21:04.763
<i>But this, too, is his decision.</i>

21:04.846 --> 21:05.681
It's a deer!

21:05.764 --> 21:07.266
<i>Having lost my battle…</i>

21:07.349 --> 21:08.308
Is it a cosplay?

21:08.392 --> 21:11.853
<i>…all I can do is trust in him</i>
<i>and see his plan through.</i>

21:12.437 --> 21:13.480
SAKAMOTO'S

21:13.563 --> 21:16.191
There's no telling what dangers await.

21:16.275 --> 21:17.192
PAYCHECK

21:17.276 --> 21:19.695
I wish I could have taken my lady back.

21:20.445 --> 21:22.406
You should try and escape as soon as--

21:22.489 --> 21:25.367
So, if we can come into contact with them,

21:25.450 --> 21:28.412
we might be able
to get information on Slur.

21:28.495 --> 21:29.329
Right.

21:29.413 --> 21:30.497
Huh?

21:30.580 --> 21:34.001
It'd be best if we can deal with them
before the JAA finds them.

21:34.084 --> 21:36.712
I'll contact Heisuke in case we need him.

21:36.795 --> 21:39.923
What the… Did none of you hear me?

21:40.007 --> 21:42.050
They're psychotic murderers.

21:42.134 --> 21:45.178
They're a totally different breed
than hit men or mafia.

21:45.262 --> 21:47.597
One wrong move and it'll be your end--

21:47.681 --> 21:48.515
If so,

21:50.225 --> 21:53.228
that's all the more reason
we can't leave them at large.

23:20.941 --> 23:25.946
Subtitle translation by: Yuka Kristi
